    "return_basis": "The served object is the Yang model-design daily series: one row per model code and date, carrying the model return and three benchmark columns (the index benchmark return, its alias benchmark_return, and the ETF blend). Each value is already a daily return as a decimal: every value is below 0.1 in magnitude, the daily scale and not a level. The four stems take the producer's codes UST (Ultra-Short Term), ST (Short Term), INT (Intermediate Term) and LT (Long Term) on the index benchmark return column, the basis the served read names; the fifth code ULT (Ultra-Long Term) is not used. The served object holds a row for each weekday, including 25 exchange holidays; those dates are dropped so that one return remains per trading day (615 per stem), and no return is interpolated. A window return is the product of one plus each daily return in the window, minus one."
